        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Fall of Constantinople</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">Siege of 53 days from 6 April to 29 May 1453; the city was taken on 29 May</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosphorus">Bosphorus</a>; the fighting centred on the Theodosian land walls, especially the Mesoteichion and the Blachernae district, and on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horn">Golden Horn</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> under Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-xi-palaiologos">Constantine XI Palaiologos</a>, with Genoese, Venetian and other foreign help: about 7,000 men, 2,000 of them foreigners by one count, and under 8,000 by Sphrantzes' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/census">census</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a>: some 50,000 to 80,000 men by recent studies, against 160,000 to 300,000 in Western witnesses.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took the city after a final assault on 29 May. It was looted for part of three days, many of its people were killed or enslaved, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed</a> made it his capital. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-xi-palaiologos">Constantine XI</a>'s fate is unknown.</span></div>
        </div>
